For aligned-panel ARC tasks, never infer the output from a single sparse feature or collapse colors into foreground/background prematurely. Record each panel's literal colors and backgrounds, then evaluate candidate cellwise rules (literal equality, same-color coincidence, panel-specific marker masks, union/intersection, and recoloring) against every output cell of every demo. Include positions where output uses its default/background color as constraints; mismatches invalidate a candidate.

